WEBVTT

00:00:19.230 --> 00:00:20.660
He will be here soon...

00:00:28.860 --> 00:00:31.170
To the world of the Phi-Brain.

00:00:46.520 --> 00:00:47.940
Kaito...

00:01:15.590 --> 00:01:17.890
Kimi no nounai e to shinnyuu
Gonna infiltrate your brain

00:01:17.890 --> 00:01:20.680
Nemutteru suki ni baby, open the gate
While you're sleeping, baby, open the gate

00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:22.470
Fukuzatsusugi security
Too-complicated security

00:01:22.470 --> 00:01:25.230
Kakusareru to abakitakunaru
When something's hidden, it makes me want to expose it

00:01:25.230 --> 00:01:29.730
Barabara ni chirabatte iru password o hiroiatsume
I'll gather up those loose, scattered passwords

00:01:29.730 --> 00:01:34.440
Kakushin ni sematte yuku, sono shoutai o misete
And approach the core, so show me that true form

00:01:34.440 --> 00:01:36.650
Kantan ni clear dekinai
I can't clear it easily

00:01:36.650 --> 00:01:39.320
Saki nante motto yomenai
Can read what lies ahead even less

00:01:39.320 --> 00:01:41.330
Kaidoku fukanou smile
A smile that can't be deciphered

00:01:41.330 --> 00:01:43.620
Kiken na puzzle
A dangerous puzzle

00:01:43.620 --> 00:01:45.580
Lock sareteta door aru nara
If there's a door that's been locked

00:01:45.580 --> 00:01:48.370
Zutto tataite miru beki, kaza-ana hiraku wa
You must keep striking it, a crack will open

00:01:48.370 --> 00:01:52.920
Eien ni hodokenai nazo nanka wa nai
No mystery remains unsolved forever

00:01:52.920 --> 00:01:55.170
Makiokosu, it's a supernova!
It's forming, it's a supernova!

00:01:55.170 --> 00:01:59.840
Tobikiri shigekiteki na hirameki o agemashou
I will give you thoroughly stimulating insight

00:01:59.840 --> 00:02:02.100
Misskey-misskey la-tu-ma

00:02:02.100 --> 00:02:04.430
Yume no naka, it's a supernova!
In the middle of a dream, it's a supernova!

00:02:04.430 --> 00:02:07.060
Watashi wa, sou, brain diver
I am, yes, a brain diver

00:02:07.060 --> 00:02:12.940
Kimi ga sagashimotometeru kotae ni nareru made
Until I become familiar with the answer you seek

00:02:15.610 --> 00:02:18.610
Brain diver

00:02:20.360 --> 00:02:23.410
Brain diver

00:02:28.040 --> 00:02:32.000
That Which Inherits Principles

00:02:38.740 --> 00:02:41.790
Jin. This is where you've been.

00:02:41.790 --> 00:02:58.020
There 184,467,447,379,486,079 remaining.

00:02:58.020 --> 00:03:01.290
Just a little more time, and
I can solve it.

00:03:01.700 --> 00:03:03.660
Jin. What are you...?

00:03:06.610 --> 00:03:07.660
That's enough.

00:03:08.310 --> 00:03:12.030
You've done enough. You can stop now.

00:03:14.880 --> 00:03:17.500
This is... punishment?

00:03:17.500 --> 00:03:20.130
For one who attempted to reach God.

00:03:20.900 --> 00:03:23.260
He ain't in this alone, y'know!

00:03:23.820 --> 00:03:25.200
Gammon.

00:03:25.200 --> 00:03:26.890
You sure keep a lot of secrets.

00:03:27.730 --> 00:03:30.410
This time, I'm gonna have
you spit 'em all out.

00:03:30.410 --> 00:03:32.420
Who the hell is this guy?

00:03:33.340 --> 00:03:36.220
He is Jin Makata.

00:03:36.220 --> 00:03:38.730
My one and only friend.

00:03:39.140 --> 00:03:42.810
The man who was once closest
to becoming a Phi-Brain.

00:03:52.320 --> 00:03:53.350
That was...

00:03:55.420 --> 00:03:59.120
It was a future where the
Puzzle of God was solved?

00:04:01.840 --> 00:04:04.310
Who is that guy?

00:04:08.350 --> 00:04:09.520
Kaito?

00:04:11.590 --> 00:04:14.440
Nonoha? Get outta here.

00:04:16.070 --> 00:04:17.820
If you want me to go, then challenge me.

00:04:18.460 --> 00:04:19.440
Challenge?

00:04:19.440 --> 00:04:22.890
If I lose, I'll leave you alone for good.

00:04:24.300 --> 00:04:25.410
Fine.

00:04:29.200 --> 00:04:30.660
Bastard!

00:04:31.740 --> 00:04:33.290
I win!

00:04:33.290 --> 00:04:35.940
That wasn't even a puzzle challenge!

00:04:35.940 --> 00:04:37.540
Of course not!

00:04:37.540 --> 00:04:40.190
There's no way
I could beat you at puzzles.

00:04:40.190 --> 00:04:41.660
Jeez, you're an idiot!

00:04:42.750 --> 00:04:44.850
Call me an idiot or a moron, that's fine.

00:04:44.850 --> 00:04:46.520
I may not be able to solve puzzles,

00:04:46.520 --> 00:04:48.930
but there are things I CAN do.

00:04:54.180 --> 00:04:55.190
Nonoha...

00:04:55.770 --> 00:04:58.160
I'm not leaving you, Kaito.

00:04:58.680 --> 00:05:01.020
There's no way I'm leaving you!

00:05:01.020 --> 00:05:05.150
I won, so now you gotta what I say!

00:05:05.540 --> 00:05:08.260
I hope you'll pardon the intrusion.

00:05:08.260 --> 00:05:09.830
Upperclassman Jikukawa!

00:05:11.300 --> 00:05:14.410
Kaito. There's something
I want to show you.

00:05:21.310 --> 00:05:24.190
This is the POG's central server?

00:05:24.190 --> 00:05:27.290
Yes. I had to go through a ton of

00:05:27.290 --> 00:05:30.680
security puzzles to get here.

00:05:30.680 --> 00:05:32.040
But...

00:05:32.040 --> 00:05:34.800
Cubik solved all of them.

00:05:35.990 --> 00:05:38.380
He did it by himself.

00:05:38.380 --> 00:05:40.420
For you, Kaito.

00:05:42.130 --> 00:05:44.440
That's awesome, Cube!

00:05:44.440 --> 00:05:47.550
W-Well, if I just use my head,

00:05:47.550 --> 00:05:49.660
something like this is a matter of course.

00:05:51.190 --> 00:05:52.300
Cubik.

00:05:54.320 --> 00:05:55.660
Thanks.

00:05:57.030 --> 00:05:58.170
Yeah.

00:05:58.590 --> 00:06:00.720
Now then, this is foreign territory,

00:06:00.720 --> 00:06:03.890
known only to the POG's top ranks.

00:06:04.720 --> 00:06:06.970
Are you ready to know the truth about

00:06:06.970 --> 00:06:09.350
the POG and the Puzzle of God?

00:06:09.350 --> 00:06:10.550
Of course.

00:06:10.890 --> 00:06:13.960
Hold on. First, tell me:

00:06:13.960 --> 00:06:16.450
Kaito, just what have you seen recently?

00:06:20.530 --> 00:06:21.970
Come on, Kaito.

00:06:22.500 --> 00:06:25.110
I saw... the future.

00:06:25.110 --> 00:06:25.860
The future?

00:06:26.300 --> 00:06:30.610
It was probably... the
death of this world.

00:06:41.810 --> 00:06:44.130
The end of the world.

00:06:47.330 --> 00:06:50.420
What? You saw the future?

00:06:51.270 --> 00:06:53.780
And the world was destroyed?

00:06:54.240 --> 00:06:57.630
This may be a result
of the massive increase

00:06:57.630 --> 00:07:00.020
in your thought processing speed.

00:07:00.430 --> 00:07:03.270
Still, something like that is just...

00:07:04.050 --> 00:07:05.700
It's possible.

00:07:05.700 --> 00:07:09.280
The Armlet of Orpheus
holds that much power.

00:07:09.620 --> 00:07:13.530
If someone gets their hands on the
Book of God,

00:07:13.530 --> 00:07:15.110
the future will end up like that.

00:07:15.730 --> 00:07:17.430
That's what Jin said.

00:07:17.430 --> 00:07:19.790
"Someone"? But who?

00:07:20.040 --> 00:07:25.540
It could be the leader of the POG,
Count Pythagoras.

00:07:27.800 --> 00:07:30.510
That man is obsessed
with the Puzzle of God.

00:07:40.910 --> 00:07:42.760
So, our director, Rook,

00:07:42.760 --> 00:07:45.230
was a Phi-Brain child as well, eh?

00:07:48.130 --> 00:07:50.560
I've finally seen it,

00:07:50.560 --> 00:07:53.810
what Count Pythagoras is really after.

00:07:53.810 --> 00:07:55.450
What do you mean?

00:07:55.450 --> 00:07:56.740
That SOB Rook
had a

00:07:56.740 --> 00:07:59.560
"pact" with the Armlet of Orpheus, too?

00:08:00.510 --> 00:08:01.490
Yes.

00:08:02.090 --> 00:08:04.750
There is more than one
Armlet of Orpheus.

00:08:05.600 --> 00:08:07.760
They've been discovered
all over the world.

00:08:07.760 --> 00:08:11.560
There is no precise count
of how many there are.

00:08:12.610 --> 00:08:14.710
There ain't just one?

00:08:14.710 --> 00:08:18.510
Then who made the damn things?

00:08:19.230 --> 00:08:23.020
None remain who know the answer to that.

00:08:24.610 --> 00:08:27.820
The Armlets of Orpheus were excavated.

00:08:28.500 --> 00:08:33.990
The first was found 2,300
years ago by us POG.

00:08:34.790 --> 00:08:36.650
Devices made by human hands that

00:08:36.650 --> 00:08:40.150
raise brain activity to its
highest possible level…

00:08:40.150 --> 00:08:43.040
Such are the Armlets of Orpheus.

00:08:44.010 --> 00:08:45.530
Their intended use and

00:08:45.530 --> 00:08:48.500
method of manufacture
are completely unknown.

00:08:48.500 --> 00:08:51.810
However, they have come
to be used for the

00:08:51.810 --> 00:08:55.540
ultimate goal of obtaining the Book of God.

00:08:56.620 --> 00:08:59.830
Givers and Solvers that have
become Phi-Brains

00:08:59.830 --> 00:09:02.990
clash with all the power
at their disposal.

00:09:02.990 --> 00:09:06.020
Truly, that is the one and only way

00:09:06.020 --> 00:09:09.230
that will open the door to the Puzzle of God.

00:09:09.690 --> 00:09:11.070
So, in other words....

00:09:11.370 --> 00:09:13.600
Yes. The Count intends to

00:09:13.600 --> 00:09:17.070
make Kaito and Rook battle each other.

00:09:18.210 --> 00:09:21.480
He's attempting to recreate it:

00:09:21.480 --> 00:09:26.270
the ritual that two years ago,
with Jin and I,

00:09:26.270 --> 00:09:27.690
failed to reach fruition.

00:09:28.290 --> 00:09:29.080
Jin!

00:09:32.470 --> 00:09:33.800
Jin Makata.

00:09:33.800 --> 00:09:37.730
He, too, is a holder
of an Armlet of Orpheus,

00:09:37.730 --> 00:09:40.710
his fate shaped by Count Pythagoras.

00:09:43.410 --> 00:09:44.850
I've solved it, Baron.

00:09:47.890 --> 00:09:51.330
This was the final duel of our life
at the academy,

00:09:51.330 --> 00:09:53.610
yet I lose again, eh?

00:09:53.610 --> 00:09:56.490
You truly can solve any puzzle, Jin.

00:09:57.500 --> 00:09:59.830
What kind of downbeat talk is that?

00:09:59.830 --> 00:10:02.490
We're going to enter the POG.

00:10:03.460 --> 00:10:04.500
Yeah.

00:10:04.500 --> 00:10:07.010
You have to strive to
be the very best Giver.

00:10:07.010 --> 00:10:09.500
I'll be the pinnacle of a Solver.

00:10:09.840 --> 00:10:12.250
The pinnacle... of a Solver?

00:10:12.740 --> 00:10:14.400
A Phi-Brain.

00:10:15.510 --> 00:10:17.760
I'll become a Phi-Brain.

00:10:18.220 --> 00:10:21.830
And... I'll solve the
Puzzle of God, for sure.

00:10:24.420 --> 00:10:25.850
There is no other reason

00:10:25.850 --> 00:10:29.770
you two were admitted into the POG.

00:10:30.110 --> 00:10:32.260
Solve the Puzzle of God

00:10:32.260 --> 00:10:35.440
and obtain the Book of God...

00:10:35.440 --> 00:10:38.630
to usher in a new era for mankind.

00:10:38.630 --> 00:10:39.660
Jin Makata.

00:10:40.010 --> 00:10:41.540
S-Sir!

00:10:41.540 --> 00:10:43.670
I'm counting on you.

00:10:56.890 --> 00:10:59.800
As a Solver, Jin's admittance to the POG

00:10:59.800 --> 00:11:02.080
was an exception to the extreme.

00:11:02.850 --> 00:11:06.480
That's just how unparalleled
his abilities were.

00:11:07.130 --> 00:11:10.770
I didn't realize that
at the time, however.

00:11:11.080 --> 00:11:13.280
In order to spur Jin's growth,

00:11:13.280 --> 00:11:15.660
I was ordered to be his personal

00:11:15.660 --> 00:11:18.050
Giver and make his puzzles.

00:11:18.510 --> 00:11:20.200
But in time,

00:11:20.200 --> 00:11:24.530
Jin became unable
to be satisfied with that.

00:11:29.230 --> 00:11:32.090
With the powers at his disposal,

00:11:32.090 --> 00:11:37.110
he began to
challenge more dangerous puzzles...

00:11:45.050 --> 00:11:47.040
The Philosopher's Puzzles.

00:11:47.690 --> 00:11:49.730
And then one day, it happened.

00:11:50.000 --> 00:11:52.710
He saw the future.

00:11:57.380 --> 00:11:58.550
What's that?

00:12:09.220 --> 00:12:12.960
C-Count Pythagoras!

00:12:19.840 --> 00:12:21.580
Don't talk foolishness!

00:12:21.580 --> 00:12:22.760
It's true.

00:12:24.220 --> 00:12:26.400
I saw it, for sure:

00:12:26.400 --> 00:12:27.800
A future where Count

00:12:27.800 --> 00:12:29.520
Pythagoras destroys the world.

00:12:29.990 --> 00:12:32.430
It was just an illusion!

00:12:32.430 --> 00:12:34.020
Count Pythagoras wants the Book of God

00:12:34.020 --> 00:12:35.500
to make a better future for-

00:12:35.500 --> 00:12:37.540
Through the ages, many men

00:12:37.540 --> 00:12:39.540
have wanted the Book of God.

00:12:39.540 --> 00:12:40.930
So that they could use

00:12:40.930 --> 00:12:43.760
its power to make
the world their own.

00:12:44.710 --> 00:12:46.160
The Count is no different.

00:12:46.350 --> 00:12:47.190
But-

00:12:47.190 --> 00:12:50.910
Baron, the Count has fooled us!

00:12:52.740 --> 00:12:55.460
I'm... giving up puzzles.

00:12:55.460 --> 00:12:56.210
Jin!

00:12:56.750 --> 00:12:59.430
I can't let him get his way!

00:12:59.430 --> 00:13:02.200
If I give up
on puzzles, that'll be the end of it.

00:13:02.710 --> 00:13:04.720
But Jin! You...

00:13:05.550 --> 00:13:08.220
It's okay. I'm okay with this.

00:13:15.770 --> 00:13:18.050
Damn you, Jin Makata!

00:13:18.050 --> 00:13:20.760
The Count's anger was fierce.

00:13:20.760 --> 00:13:23.470
But that just proved that

00:13:23.470 --> 00:13:25.950
what Jin said had been right.

00:13:27.450 --> 00:13:30.950
I remained in the POG. In fact...

00:13:32.360 --> 00:13:35.050
You have proven your worth as a Giver.

00:13:35.050 --> 00:13:37.700
I order you to transfer to Section Phi.

00:13:37.700 --> 00:13:38.960
Thank you very much.

00:13:39.530 --> 00:13:43.960
By my hands, I WILL
cultivate the Phi-Brain.

00:13:44.550 --> 00:13:47.260
If so, then... Here is
your first assignment.

00:13:51.870 --> 00:13:55.310
I leave this child to you.

00:13:55.840 --> 00:13:56.770
Sir.

00:14:01.030 --> 00:14:02.370
Who's that boy?

00:14:02.370 --> 00:14:04.150
Kaito Daimon.

00:14:04.150 --> 00:14:06.530
A Phi-Brain child, like you.

00:14:06.870 --> 00:14:08.260
A Phi-Brain?

00:14:08.760 --> 00:14:10.530
A youngster like HIM?

00:14:11.010 --> 00:14:14.430
His potential was noted since the moment
he was born.

00:14:14.430 --> 00:14:17.420
He has been raised by the POG.

00:14:17.770 --> 00:14:19.170
What of his parents?

00:14:19.850 --> 00:14:21.920
They were nuisances, and disposed of.

00:14:23.440 --> 00:14:26.370
And this is what you're doing now?

00:14:26.370 --> 00:14:26.920
Yes.

00:14:30.980 --> 00:14:34.270
What do you think it took
for me to give up puzzles?!

00:14:34.270 --> 00:14:35.470
And yet you...!

00:14:36.350 --> 00:14:37.670
Look who's talking!

00:14:37.670 --> 00:14:39.480
You think you know me?!

00:14:41.950 --> 00:14:45.020
The Count hasn't given up
on the Book of God.

00:14:45.020 --> 00:14:47.110
To crush his ambitions,

00:14:47.110 --> 00:14:49.450
I'm going to find
the Book first and

00:14:49.450 --> 00:14:51.120
rid this world of it.

00:14:51.120 --> 00:14:52.870
There's no other way!

00:14:53.740 --> 00:14:57.370
All we can do is entrust
the future to that boy.

00:14:57.960 --> 00:15:00.280
I understand how you feel.

00:15:00.280 --> 00:15:01.870
When I look at that boy,

00:15:01.870 --> 00:15:03.380
I think of how you used to be.

00:15:04.120 --> 00:15:06.380
That boy loves puzzles, too.

00:15:16.730 --> 00:15:17.930
Stupid puzzles.

00:15:22.050 --> 00:15:23.080
You fine with that?

00:15:25.920 --> 00:15:27.490
You really liked them, right?

00:15:27.490 --> 00:15:29.070
You're okay with giving them up?

00:15:29.790 --> 00:15:31.880
Even if you do, you can't escape

00:15:31.880 --> 00:15:35.450
the sadness of having
lost something dear.

00:15:36.750 --> 00:15:39.010
Don't give up what is dear.

00:15:40.380 --> 00:15:41.530
Never.

00:15:45.450 --> 00:15:49.300
Jin from without, and me from within...

00:15:49.740 --> 00:15:51.860
We had begun working to

00:15:51.860 --> 00:15:54.300
crush the Count's ambitions.

00:15:56.560 --> 00:15:59.820
Right now, I still can't beat the Count.

00:15:59.820 --> 00:16:01.980
But the next time I return...

00:16:03.090 --> 00:16:04.980
That boy will have no part of it.

00:16:05.980 --> 00:16:09.440
Jin embarked on a long, dangerous

00:16:09.440 --> 00:16:12.490
pilgrimage of Puzzles of Fools.

00:16:57.400 --> 00:16:59.370
Baron Kaidou.

00:16:59.370 --> 00:17:03.660
I appoint you
leader of Section Phi.

00:17:04.870 --> 00:17:06.870
Incidentally, it seems someone

00:17:06.870 --> 00:17:10.810
has been
releasing Puzzles of Fools recently.

00:17:10.810 --> 00:17:15.180
It is not worth paying
such rabble any mind.

00:17:16.210 --> 00:17:18.180
Well, so be it.

00:17:18.700 --> 00:17:23.140
I was raising the true Phi-Brain.

00:17:25.690 --> 00:17:27.710
Jin had come to England,

00:17:27.710 --> 00:17:29.690
and explained that he'd once

00:17:29.690 --> 00:17:31.610
again made contact with Kaito.

00:17:32.080 --> 00:17:34.940
Then, two years ago...

00:17:37.900 --> 00:17:38.770
Baron.

00:17:43.410 --> 00:17:44.620
The time has come.

00:17:45.670 --> 00:17:47.280
It seems that Count Pythagoras

00:17:47.280 --> 00:17:49.530
has learned where the Puzzle of God is.

00:17:50.730 --> 00:17:51.670
Will you go?

00:17:52.060 --> 00:17:53.830
The Puzzle of God can only

00:17:53.830 --> 00:17:56.700
be solved if Pythagoras and I fight.

00:17:57.140 --> 00:18:01.430
Then, the survivor can obtain
the Book of God.

00:18:02.060 --> 00:18:04.330
His power is vast.

00:18:04.330 --> 00:18:05.190
I'm sure.

00:18:05.190 --> 00:18:08.940
A puzzle where, in the end,
one must be sacrificed.

00:18:08.940 --> 00:18:10.480
If you lose, your life will be-

00:18:10.480 --> 00:18:11.400
I know.

00:18:12.210 --> 00:18:13.940
Jin. I...

00:18:15.670 --> 00:18:18.950
Baron, you have your own role to play.

00:18:19.430 --> 00:18:21.460
My role?

00:18:22.110 --> 00:18:24.290
Ridding this world of the Book of God.

00:18:26.680 --> 00:18:29.040
Bring this chain of tragedies to a close.

00:18:29.630 --> 00:18:31.540
That's my only request.

00:18:35.760 --> 00:18:36.550
Jin!

00:18:42.690 --> 00:18:44.810
Now you know everything.

00:18:45.170 --> 00:18:46.650
Hold on!

00:18:46.650 --> 00:18:48.150
What happened with the showdown

00:18:48.150 --> 00:18:50.150
between Jin and the Count?

00:18:50.150 --> 00:18:51.250
I do not know.

00:18:51.250 --> 00:18:52.480
You don't know?!

00:18:52.930 --> 00:18:56.570
I have no memories at all of that day.

00:18:57.350 --> 00:18:59.700
But I can say this:

00:19:00.310 --> 00:19:03.490
The outcome of that fight
stole Jin's spirit.

00:19:03.640 --> 00:19:09.580
And the Count never again
showed himself to others.

00:19:10.180 --> 00:19:15.190
Now, he simply uses Rook
to convey his wishes.

00:19:16.450 --> 00:19:18.310
Still, now that things have come to this,

00:19:18.310 --> 00:19:20.990
I've been able to see the Count's motives.

00:19:21.980 --> 00:19:25.420
This time, for sure,
he intends to open it.

00:19:26.130 --> 00:19:28.270
The door to the Puzzle of God.

00:19:28.700 --> 00:19:32.210
By using Kaito and Rook.

00:19:34.380 --> 00:19:36.280
Now I know for sure!

00:19:36.960 --> 00:19:39.620
That guy is Count Pythagoras!

00:19:39.620 --> 00:19:42.530
He's the one who's been
manipulating our fates!

00:19:44.390 --> 00:19:46.490
If I beat him, this will all be finished!

00:19:47.110 --> 00:19:48.060
Hold on.

00:19:48.060 --> 00:19:50.250
It looks like there's
another hidden file.

00:19:53.670 --> 00:19:56.020
Th-This is...!

00:19:57.040 --> 00:19:59.420
Count Pythagoras is dead?!

00:19:59.630 --> 00:20:01.400
Impossible!

00:20:01.400 --> 00:20:03.700
Then who is it that's
been issuing directives,

00:20:03.700 --> 00:20:06.060
leading the POG this whole time?!

00:20:06.700 --> 00:20:08.630
I-It can't be!

00:20:08.630 --> 00:20:10.350
Yes. Yes, it can.

00:20:15.630 --> 00:20:16.980
Rook, sir!

00:20:16.980 --> 00:20:18.730
What are you doing here?!

00:20:19.480 --> 00:20:22.390
Count Pythagoras is no more.

00:20:22.390 --> 00:20:25.740
I thought I'd tell you that, Kaito.

00:20:26.120 --> 00:20:27.710
What do you mean, he's "no more"?

00:20:27.710 --> 00:20:28.620
So...

00:20:29.130 --> 00:20:32.720
Count Pythagoras died six months ago.

00:20:34.630 --> 00:20:38.310
Currently, the one holding
all the power within

00:20:38.310 --> 00:20:39.710
the POG is ME.

00:20:40.140 --> 00:20:42.360
Rook. What are you...?

00:20:42.360 --> 00:20:47.220
There's nothing I don't mind
you knowing anymore.

00:20:49.470 --> 00:20:50.930
Even my prized possession.

00:20:51.980 --> 00:20:53.550
I'll show it to you.

00:20:58.640 --> 00:20:59.570
Jin!

00:20:59.990 --> 00:21:01.910
That's Jin Makata?

00:21:06.740 --> 00:21:07.540
Jin...

00:21:08.290 --> 00:21:11.450
That's my very special prize.

00:21:12.300 --> 00:21:13.600
Rook, you bastard!

00:21:13.600 --> 00:21:16.670
Now, now. That won't do, Kaito.

00:21:16.980 --> 00:21:17.790
Huh?!

00:21:18.130 --> 00:21:21.260
If you can't keep your
emotions under control,

00:21:21.260 --> 00:21:22.630
we can't very well call you a

00:21:22.630 --> 00:21:24.900
legitimate keeper of an Armlet, can we?

00:21:24.900 --> 00:21:27.140
Jin would be disappointed.

00:21:27.640 --> 00:21:30.230
What are you talking about?!

00:21:33.070 --> 00:21:34.400
I'll show you.

00:21:37.340 --> 00:21:38.320
That eye!

00:21:38.810 --> 00:21:40.570
Don't tell me, you...!

00:21:40.570 --> 00:21:41.570
That's right.

00:21:42.020 --> 00:21:45.170
I have a pact with an
Amulet of Orpheus, too.

00:21:45.170 --> 00:21:47.320
I'm a Phi-Brain.

00:21:48.590 --> 00:21:49.890
I don't believe it!

00:21:49.890 --> 00:21:52.330
If Count Pythagoras is dead, then...

00:21:54.810 --> 00:21:55.840
Who...

00:21:57.960 --> 00:21:59.560
Who was that?

00:22:07.660 --> 00:22:09.300
Hey, you!

00:22:18.000 --> 00:22:20.080
Me? Why?!

00:22:37.240 --> 00:22:41.540
Tsukue no ue de umareta sekai
A world born on top of a desk

00:22:41.540 --> 00:22:47.340
Ichiban saki ni kimi ni misetakatta
I wanted to show it to you first of all

00:22:47.770 --> 00:22:52.090
Karappo no heya sotto nukedashite
I sneaked silently out of that empty room

00:22:52.090 --> 00:22:57.210
Hashirihajimeteta
And started running

00:22:58.290 --> 00:23:02.610
Iki hazumasete oka o noboru to
Breathing heavily, I climbed the hill

00:23:02.610 --> 00:23:08.220
Kimi ga saki ni tsuite matte ita ne
And you were already there, waiting

00:23:08.900 --> 00:23:13.160
Takusan no hajimete kimi to mitsuketa
There were so many treasures that I first

00:23:13.160 --> 00:23:17.910
Takaramono datta
Discovered with you

00:23:18.410 --> 00:23:24.020
Kanashisa de afureta toki wa
That time when I was overcome with sadness

00:23:24.020 --> 00:23:26.600
Nanimo iwazu ni tada
You said nothing

00:23:26.600 --> 00:23:29.250
Soba ni ite kureta ne
Just stayed there by my side, didn't you?

00:23:29.250 --> 00:23:33.910
Imademo wasurenai yo
Even now, I haven't forgotten

00:23:33.910 --> 00:23:39.180
Mata aou ne, yakusoku o shiyou
Let's meet again, let's make it a promise

00:23:39.180 --> 00:23:44.400
Kei wa shinai, ano hi no sayonara
It won't fade, the "goodbye" of that day

00:23:44.400 --> 00:23:50.050
Boku no subete, kimi ga kureta michi
Everything I have, the path you gave me

00:23:50.050 --> 00:23:58.960
Zutto kokoro no naka hikaru yo
Will always shine within my heart

00:24:02.790 --> 00:24:04.860
I've been looking for you, Nonoha.

00:24:04.860 --> 00:24:06.240
You've come to scout me?!

00:24:06.240 --> 00:24:07.440
Wow, no way!

00:24:07.440 --> 00:24:08.970
Is it time for my celebrity debut?

00:24:08.970 --> 00:24:10.170
You've got it all wrong.

00:24:10.170 --> 00:24:11.500
I wanted to ask how to

00:24:11.500 --> 00:24:13.260
stop those two puzzle-loving idiots.

00:24:13.260 --> 00:24:14.990
Oh. Kaito and Gammon?

00:24:14.990 --> 00:24:15.870
That's right.

00:24:15.870 --> 00:24:18.140
At this rate, things
won't end well for either of them.

00:24:18.640 --> 00:24:21.270
Next time: "The Choice Left Remaining"

00:24:20.870 --> 00:24:27.500
The Choice Left Remaining

00:24:21.640 --> 00:24:23.190
I'm sure they'll be fine.

00:24:23.190 --> 00:24:24.650
They may be idiots,

00:24:24.650 --> 00:24:26.530
but they don't forget what's important.
